{"id":"mahabharata-8-029","work":"mahabharata","part":8,"partName":"कर्णपर्व","partNameEn":"Karna Parva","unit":29,"title":"एकोनत्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 29 · Karna answers Shalya","summary":{"en":"Karna, displeased, answers Shalya that he knows Arjuna's might and still will fight him, and tells him of his own divine weapons. He rebukes Shalya for insulting his friend and says he will not be moved by his words.","kn":"ಅಸಮಾಧಾನಗೊಂಡ ಕರ್ಣ ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಬಲ ತಿಳಿದಿದ್ದರೂ ಹೋರಾಡುವೆನೆಂದು ಶಲ್ಯನಿಗೆ ಉತ್ತರಿಸಿ ತನ್ನ ದಿವ್ಯಾಸ್ತ್ರಗಳನ್ನು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಗೆಳೆಯನನ್ನು ಅವಮಾನಿಸಿದ ಶಲ್ಯನನ್ನು ಖಂಡಿಸಿ ಅವನ ಮಾತಿಗೆ ಬಗ್ಗುವುದಿಲ್ಲವೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"असन्तुष्ट कर्ण शल्य को उत्तर देता है कि वह अर्जुन का बल जानता है फिर भी उससे लड़ेगा, और अपने दिव्यास्त्रों का वर्णन करता है। वह मित्र का अपमान करने पर शल्य को फटकारता है और कहता है कि उसकी बातों से विचलित नहीं होगा।","te":"అసంతృప్తి చెందిన కర్ణుడు అర్జునుని బలం తెలిసినా పోరాడతానని శల్యునికి బదులిచ్చి తన దివ్యాస్త్రాలను చెబుతాడు. మిత్రుని అవమానించినందుకు శల్యుని గద్దించి అతని మాటలకు కదలనని అంటాడు.","ta":"அதிருப்தியுற்ற கர்ணன் அர்ஜுனனின் ஆற்றல் தெரிந்தும் அவனுடன் போரிடுவேன் என்று சல்யனுக்குப் பதிலளித்துத் தன் தெய்வ அஸ்திரங்களைக் கூறுகிறான். நண்பனை இகழ்ந்ததற்காகச் சல்யனைக் கடிந்து, அவன் பேச்சால் அசைய மாட்டேன் என்கிறான்.","ml":"കോപിച്ച കർണ്ണൻ, അർജുനന്റെ ശക്തി അറിഞ്ഞിട്ടും അദ്ദേഹത്തെ നേരിടുമെന്ന് ശല്യനോട് പറയുന്നു; തന്റെ ദിവ്യായുധങ്ങളെക്കുറിച്ചും സംസാരിക്കുന്നു. തന്റെ സുഹൃത്തിനെ അപമാനിച്ചതിന് ശല്യനെ ശാസിക്കുന്ന അദ്ദേഹം, ആ വാക്കുകൾ തന്നെ ഇളക്കില്ലെന്ന് പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 8.29; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 29 2019","sections":[{"title":"कर्णपर्व","titleEn":"Karna Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"मद्राधिपस्याधिरथिस्तदैवं\nवचो निशम्याप्रियमप्रतीतः ।\nउवाच शल्यं विदितं ममैत-\nद्यथाविधावर्जुनवासुदेवौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the lord of Madra's unpleasant words, Adhiratha's son was displeased and said to Shalya: \"I know well what kind of men Arjuna and Vasudeva are.\""}},{"n":2,"text":"शौरे रथं वाहयतोऽर्जुनस्य\nबलं महास्त्राणि च पाण्डवस्य ।\nअहं विजानामि यथावदद्य\nपरोक्षभूतं तव तत्तु शल्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Shalya, I know exactly, today, the strength and great weapons of the Pandava Arjuna, as Krishna drives his chariot, though these remain unseen by you.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"तौ चाप्रधृष्यौ शस्त्रभृतां वरिष्ठौ\nव्यपेतभीर्योधयिष्यामि कृष्णौ ।\nसंतापयत्यभ्यधिकं तु रामा-\nच्छापोऽद्य मां ब्राह्मणसत्तमाच्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Those two Krishnas, unassailable and best of weapon-bearers, I shall fight without fear. Yet the curse of Rama and of that best of brahmins torments me greatly today.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"अवात्सं वै ब्राह्मणच्छद्मनाहं\nरामे पुरा दिव्यमस्त्रं चिकीर्षुः ।\nतत्रापि मे देवराजेन विघ्नो\nहितार्थिना फल्गुनस्यैव शल्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Long ago, Shalya, wanting a divine weapon from Rama, I lived with him in the disguise of a brahmin. Even there the king of the gods, wishing Phalguna's good, put an obstacle in my way.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"कृतोऽवभेदेन ममोरुमेत्य\nप्रविश्य कीटस्य तनुं विरूपाम् ।\nगुरोर्भयाच्चापि न चेलिवानहं\nतच्चावबुद्धो ददृशे स विप्रः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He came and split my thigh, entering it in the deformed body of an insect. Out of fear of my teacher I did not stir, and that brahmin awoke and saw it.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"पृष्टश्चाहं तमवोचं महर्षिं\nसूतोऽहमस्मीति स मां शशाप ।\nसूतोपधावाप्तमिदं त्वयास्त्रं\nन कर्मकाले प्रतिभास्यति त्वाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Questioned, I told that great sage, 'I am a charioteer's son,' and he cursed me: 'This weapon you obtained by posing as a charioteer's son will not come to your mind when its time of use arrives.'\""}},{"n":7,"text":"अन्यत्र यस्मात्तव मृत्युकाला-\nदब्राह्मणे ब्रह्म न हि ध्रुवं स्यात् ।\nतदद्य पर्याप्तमतीव शस्त्र-\nमस्मिन्संग्रामे तुमुले तात भीमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Except at the time of your death, since Brahma's weapon cannot stay firm in one who is not a brahmin.' So now, my friend, that weapon is quite enough in this terrible, tumultuous battle.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"अपां पतिर्वेगवानप्रमेयो\nनिमज्जयिष्यन्निवहान्प्रजानाम् ।\nमहानगं यः कुरुते समुद्रं\nवेलैव तं वारयत्यप्रमेयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The swift, immeasurable lord of waters would drown the multitudes of creatures if he could make the great sea a mountain, but the shore holds back that boundless ocean.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"प्रमुञ्चन्तं बाणसंघानमोघा-\nन्मर्मच्छिदो वीरहणः सपत्रान् ।\nकुन्तीपुत्रं प्रतियोत्स्यामि युद्धे\nज्याकर्षिणामुत्तममद्य लोके ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I will fight in battle that son of Kunti, best of all who draw the bowstring, who looses showers of sure arrows with feathers that pierce vitals and slay heroes.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"एवं बलेनातिबलं महास्त्रं\nसमुद्रकल्पं सुदुरापमुग्रम् ।\nशरौघिणं पार्थिवान्मज्जयन्तं\nवेलेव पार्थमिषुभिः संसहिष्ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So, with my strength, I will withstand Partha, a great-weapon wielder of excessive power, terrible and hard to reach like an ocean, who sinks kings in floods of arrows, as the shore does the sea, with my arrows.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"अद्याहवे यस्य न तुल्यमन्यं\nमन्ये मनुष्यं धनुराददानम् ।\nसुरासुरान्वै युधि यो जयेत\nतेनाद्य मे पश्य युद्धं सुघोरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today in battle I think no other man who takes up a bow is his equal, the one who could defeat gods and asuras in combat. See my dreadful fight with him today.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"अतिमानी पाण्डवो युद्धकामो\nअमानुषैरेष्यति मे महास्त्रैः ।\nतस्यास्त्रमस्त्रैरभिहत्य संख्ये\nशरोत्तमैः पातयिष्यामि पार्थम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The overproud Pandava, eager for battle, will come at me with superhuman great weapons. Striking his weapons with mine in the fight, I will bring Partha down with the best arrows.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"दिवाकरेणापि समं तपन्तं\nसमाप्तरश्मिं यशसा ज्वलन्तम् ।\nतमोनुदं मेघ इवातिमात्रो\nधनंजयं छादयिष्यामि बाणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Though he blazes like the sun, with rays complete, shining in fame, I will cover Dhananjaya with arrows, as a great cloud hides the sun that drives away darkness.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"वैश्वानरं धूमशिखं ज्वलन्तं\nतेजस्विनं लोकमिमं दहन्तम् ।\nमेघो भूत्वा शरवर्षैर्यथाग्निं\nतथा पार्थं शमयिष्यामि युद्धे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As a cloud pours rain on a blazing fire, smoke-crested, brilliant, burning this world, so I will quench Partha in battle with showers of arrows.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"प्रमाथिनं बलवन्तं प्रहारिणं\nप्रभञ्जनं मातरिश्वानमुग्रम् ।\nयुद्धे सहिष्ये हिमवानिवाचलो\nधनंजयं क्रुद्धममृष्यमाणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Like the mountain Himalaya I will endure in battle the angry, unforgiving Dhananjaya, who crushes and strikes, powerful, like the terrible, shattering wind.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"विशारदं रथमार्गेष्वसक्तं\nधुर्यं नित्यं समरेषु प्रवीरम् ।\nलोके वरं सर्वधनुर्धराणां\nधनंजयं संयुगे संसहिष्ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I will face in combat Dhananjaya, skilled, unhindered on chariot paths, always a leader, a hero in battles, the finest of all bowmen in the world.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"अद्याहवे यस्य न तुल्यमन्यं\nमध्येमनुष्यं धनुराददानम् ।\nसर्वामिमां यः पृथिवीं सहेत\nतथा विद्वान्योत्स्यमानोऽस्मि तेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I fight today the man who has no equal, among men, as he takes up the bow, who could withstand this whole earth; I know this and still I will fight him.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"यः सर्वभूतानि सदेवकानि\nप्रस्थेऽजयत्खाण्डवे सव्यसाची ।\nको जीवितं रक्षमाणो हि तेन\nयुयुत्सते मामृते मानुषोऽन्यः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Savyasachin conquered all beings with the gods at Khandava on his own; what other man would fight him to protect his life, except me?\""}},{"n":19,"text":"अहं तस्य पौरुषं पाण्डवस्य\nब्रूयां हृष्टः समितौ क्षत्रियाणाम् ।\nकिं त्वं मूर्खः प्रभषन्मूढचेता\nमामवोचः पौरुषमर्जुनस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I could happily tell of that Pandava's manliness in an assembly of kshatriyas. Why, you fool, with your muddled mind, do you babble to me of Arjuna's manhood?\""}},{"n":20,"text":"अप्रियो यः परुषो निष्ठुरो हि\nक्षुद्रः क्षेप्ता क्षमिणश्चाक्षमावान् ।\nहन्यामहं तादृशानां शतानि\nक्षमामि त्वां क्षमया कालयोगात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I could kill hundreds of such disagreeable, harsh, cruel, mean abusers who slander patient and impatient men alike. I forgive you only through patience and the force of time.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"अवोचस्त्वं पाण्डवार्थेऽप्रियाणि\nप्रधर्षयन्मां मूढवत्पापकर्मन् ।\nमय्यार्जवे जिह्मगतिर्हतस्त्वं\nमित्रद्रोही सप्तपदं हि मित्रम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You said unpleasant things for the Pandavas' sake, attacking me like a fool, sinner. Honest with me, you take a crooked path; you are a traitor to a friend, though friendship comes with seven steps.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"कालस्त्वयं मृत्युमयोऽतिदारुणो\nदुर्योधनो युद्धमुपागमद्यत् ।\nतस्यार्थसिद्धिमभिकाङ्क्षमाण-\nस्तमभ्येष्ये यत्र नैकान्त्यमस्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This time is a dreadful one, made of death, in which Duryodhana has come to war. Wishing his success, I will go against Arjuna, where there is no certainty.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"मित्रं मिदेर्नन्दतेः प्रीयतेर्वा\nसंत्रायतेर्मानद मोदतेर्वा ।\nब्रवीति तच्चामुत विप्रपूर्वा-\nत्तच्चापि सर्वं मम दुर्योधनेऽस्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A friend (mitra) is one who is loving, or delights, or is dear, or protects, or gives joy, honorable sir, and what is said of one beginning with 'a brahmin' also; all that I find in Duryodhana.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"शत्रुः शदेः शासतेः शायतेर्वा\nशृणातेर्वा श्वयतेर्वापि सर्गे ।\nउपसर्गाद्बहुधा सूदतेश्च\nप्रायेण सर्वं त्वयि तच्च मह्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"An enemy (shatru) is one who harms, rules, destroys, or swells, as the roots and prefixes are said in many ways; for the most part all that is in you, and that is the case with me.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"दुर्योधनार्थं तव चाप्रियार्थं\nयशोर्थमात्मार्थमपीश्वरार्थम् ।\nतस्मादहं पाण्डववासुदेवौ\nयोत्स्ये यत्नात्कर्म तत्पश्य मेऽद्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"For Duryodhana's sake, and for what displeases you, for fame, for myself, and for my lord, I will therefore fight the Pandava and Vasudeva with effort. See that deed of mine today.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"अस्त्राणि पश्याद्य ममोत्तमानि\nब्राह्माणि दिव्यान्यथ मानुषाणि ।\nआसादयिष्याम्यहमुग्रवीर्यं\nद्विपोत्तमं मत्तमिवाभिमत्तः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"See my best weapons today, Brahma and divine and human ones. I will attack that fierce-valiant best of elephants, as a rutting elephant attacks another in rut.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"अस्त्रं ब्राह्मं मनसा तद्ध्यजय्यं\nक्षेप्स्ये पार्थायाप्रतिमं जयाय ।\nतेनापि मे नैव मुच्येत युद्धे\nन चेत्पतेद्विषमे मेऽद्य चक्रम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I will hurl the unconquerable Brahma weapon, matchless, from my mind at Partha for victory. Even then he would not be freed from me in battle, unless my chariot wheel falls into a pit today.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"वैवस्वताद्दण्डहस्ताद्वरुणाद्वापि पाशिनः ।\nसगदाद्वा धनपतेः सवज्राद्वापि वासवात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I am not afraid of Yama with the rod in hand, nor Varuna with the noose, nor the lord of wealth with his mace, nor Indra with the thunderbolt.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"नान्यस्मादपि कस्माच्चिद्बिभिमो ह्याततायिनः ।\nइति शल्य विजानीहि यथा नाहं बिभेम्यभीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Nor of any other armed assailant. Know this, Shalya: I am fearless.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"तस्माद्भयं न मे पार्थान्नापि चैव जनार्दनात् ।\nअद्य युद्धं हि ताभ्यां मे संपराये भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So I have no fear of Partha or Janardana. Today, in battle, my fight will be with the two of them.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"श्वभ्रे ते पततां चक्रमिति मे ब्राह्मणोऽवदत् ।\nयुध्यमानस्य संग्रामे प्राप्तस्यैकायने भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'May your wheel fall into a pit,' that brahmin told me; 'one who fights and reaches a single path will face danger.'\""}},{"n":32,"text":"तस्माद्बिभेमि बलवद्ब्राह्मणव्याहृतादहम् ।\nएते हि सोमराजान ईश्वराः सुखदुःखयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Therefore I fear greatly what the brahmin said. These Soma-kings are lords over joy and sorrow.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"होमधेन्वा वत्समस्य प्रमत्त इषुणाहनम् ।\nचरन्तमजने शल्य ब्राह्मणात्तपसो निधेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Once, careless, I killed with an arrow the calf of a sacrificial cow, while roaming in a wilderness, belonging to a brahmin, a treasury of austerity.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"ईषादन्तान्सप्तशतान्दासीदासशतानि च ।\nददतो द्विजमुख्याय प्रसादं न चकार मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I offered that chief of brahmins seven hundred elephants with pole-like tusks and hundreds of male and female servants, but he did not forgive me.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"कृष्णानां श्वेतवत्सानां सहस्राणि चतुर्दश ।\nआहरन्न लभे तस्मात्प्रसादं द्विजसत्तमात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Bringing fourteen thousand black cows with white calves, I still did not win the favor of that best of brahmins.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"ऋद्धं गेहं सर्वकामैर्यच्च मे वसु किंचन ।\nतत्सर्वमस्मै सत्कृत्य प्रयच्छामि न चेच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I offered him all the wealth and whatever I had in my house, rich with every desire, with honor; but he did not want it.\""}},{"n":37,"text":"ततोऽब्रवीन्मां याचन्तमपराद्धं प्रयत्नतः ।\nव्याहृतं यन्मया सूत तत्तथा न तदन्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then he said to me, who begged and was carefully guilty: 'What I have spoken, charioteer, will be so, not otherwise.'\""}},{"n":38,"text":"अनृतोक्तं प्रजा हन्यात्ततः पापमवाप्नुयात् ।\nतस्माद्धर्माभिरक्षार्थं नानृतं वक्तुमुत्सहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'A falsehood spoken would destroy creatures and bring sin. So to protect dharma I do not dare to say what is untrue.'\""}},{"n":39,"text":"मा त्वं ब्रह्मगतिं हिंस्याः प्रायश्चित्तं कृतं त्वया ।\nमद्वाक्यं नानृतं लोके कश्चित्कुर्यात्समाप्नुहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Do not harm the brahmin's path; you have made atonement. No one in the world could make my word false; go in peace.'\""}},{"n":40,"text":"इत्येतत्ते मया प्रोक्तं क्षिप्तेनापि सुहृत्तया ।\nजानामि त्वाधिक्षिपन्तं जोषमास्स्वोत्तरं शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"All this I have told you, though insulted, as a friend. I know you insult me; be silent, and hear my answer.\""}}]}]}